1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:08,280
Bekzod builds Malika's website, and one Wednesday he reads about web skimming and stops sleeping well.

2
00:00:08,330 --> 00:00:12,456
A thief adds one line of script to a payment page.

3
00:00:12,506 --> 00:00:18,192
It might arrive through a hacked analytics tool, or a changed file on a shared server.

4
00:00:18,242 --> 00:00:24,288
That one line copies every card number as the buyer types it, and sends it away.

5
00:00:24,338 --> 00:00:26,160
The page still works.

6
00:00:26,210 --> 00:00:28,032
The buyer still pays.

7
00:00:28,082 --> 00:00:30,336
Nobody notices for weeks.

8
00:00:30,386 --> 00:00:35,616
Bekzod writes to Timur at the bank: could this happen to Malika's buyers?

9
00:00:35,666 --> 00:00:39,096
Timur answers with an invitation: come and try.

10
00:00:39,146 --> 00:00:44,544
In Lesson 5, the card frame became the bank's card reader on the payment page.

11
00:00:44,594 --> 00:00:47,616
This lesson shows the seals on that reader.

12
00:00:47,666 --> 00:00:52,392
The frame is the card zone's own small page, on its own address.

13
00:00:52,442 --> 00:00:55,896
It sits inside the bank's payment page like a window.

14
00:00:55,946 --> 00:01:02,528
How would you stop a stranger's script from reading what is typed in that window?

15
00:01:02,578 --> 00:01:06,464
A real card reader on a shop counter has tamper seals.

16
00:01:06,514 --> 00:01:08,336
The frame has three.

17
00:01:08,386 --> 00:01:13,112
Seal one: only the page its session names may hold the frame.

18
00:01:13,162 --> 00:01:18,344
Each time a buyer pays, the card zone opens a session for one page.

19
00:01:18,394 --> 00:01:23,408
A look-alike site that tries to hold the frame is refused by the browser.

20
00:01:23,458 --> 00:01:26,744
Seal two: a Content Security Policy.

21
00:01:26,794 --> 00:01:29,816
That is a rule the frame gives the browser.

22
00:01:29,866 --> 00:01:35,912
It says: run nothing but my own two files, and talk only to my own address.

23
00:01:35,962 --> 00:01:39,440
Any other script is refused before it runs.

24
00:01:39,490 --> 00:01:43,136
Seal three: Subresource Integrity.

25
00:01:43,186 --> 00:01:47,024
The frame names each of its two files by a fingerprint.

26
00:01:47,074 --> 00:01:54,128
If even one character of a file changes, the fingerprint no longer matches, and the browser will not run it.

27
00:01:54,178 --> 00:02:01,400
When the buyer finishes, the frame hands back only two things: a token and the masked number.

28
00:02:01,450 --> 00:02:05,696
It hands them only to the one page its session names.

29
00:02:05,746 --> 00:02:08,888
The card number itself never leaves the frame.

30
00:02:08,938 --> 00:02:12,896
When the browser blocks something, it reports it to the card zone.

31
00:02:12,946 --> 00:02:16,112
So a tampering attempt leaves a trace.

32
00:02:16,162 --> 00:02:22,520
And the page around the frame is watched too, because a skimmer there could still trick the buyer.

33
00:02:22,570 --> 00:02:25,688
Then Timur and Bekzod sit down to break it.

34
00:02:25,738 --> 00:02:27,680
First, a normal payment.

35
00:02:27,730 --> 00:02:34,448
The frame appears inside the payment page, with two fields: card number and expiry date.

36
00:02:34,498 --> 00:02:38,528
As Bekzod types, the number falls into groups of four.

37
00:02:38,578 --> 00:02:42,152
The expiry date gets its slash by itself.

38
00:02:42,202 --> 00:02:47,288
He presses Send code, types the code from his phone, and presses Confirm.

39
00:02:47,338 --> 00:02:51,320
The frame says "Card accepted" and clears the number field.

40
00:02:51,370 --> 00:02:54,128
The page shows only the masked line.

41
00:02:54,178 --> 00:02:59,768
Now Bekzod opens the frame's address on its own, outside the payment page.

42
00:02:59,818 --> 00:03:05,432
It shows one sentence: this page opens only inside the payment page.

43
00:03:05,482 --> 00:03:07,304
No form appears.

44
00:03:07,354 --> 00:03:10,472
He puts the frame inside a look-alike site.

45
00:03:10,522 --> 00:03:14,360
The browser shows an empty, refused box instead.

46
00:03:14,410 --> 00:03:16,136
Then he plays the thief.

47
00:03:16,186 --> 00:03:20,696
Inside the frame, he tries to load a script from another address.

48
00:03:20,746 --> 00:03:26,864
The browser's console shows a red line: the script is refused under the frame's policy.

49
00:03:26,914 --> 00:03:28,736
Nothing loads.

50
00:03:28,786 --> 00:03:31,136
Timur turns his screen around.

51
00:03:31,186 --> 00:03:34,712
The refusal has already arrived as a report.

52
00:03:34,762 --> 00:03:40,280
It sits in the card zone's logs, with the rule that was broken and the page it came from.

53
00:03:40,330 --> 00:03:42,416
No card data is in it.

54
00:03:42,466 --> 00:03:46,544
I think this is the part of card security most people forget.

55
00:03:46,594 --> 00:03:53,216
A database can be locked and sealed, and a skimmer can still copy numbers at the keyboard.

56
00:03:53,266 --> 00:03:59,384
The one moment a card number exists in plain view is in the buyer's browser, as it is typed.

57
00:03:59,434 --> 00:04:01,304
The seals guard that moment.

58
00:04:01,354 --> 00:04:04,064
They protect the buyer from a stranger's script.

59
00:04:04,114 --> 00:04:06,680
They protect the bank from a stolen form.

60
00:04:06,730 --> 00:04:11,456
And they protect Malika, whose pages never touch the number.

61
00:04:11,506 --> 00:04:13,616
That night, Bekzod slept.

62
00:04:13,666 --> 00:04:21,416
To recap: the frame has three seals: the right page, a content rule, and file fingerprints.

63
00:04:21,466 --> 00:04:26,464
Which seal stops a script from another address?

64
00:04:26,514 --> 00:04:32,368
The content security policy: it runs only the frame's own files.

65
00:04:32,418 --> 00:04:35,584
Next: the two doors into the locked room.
